=== 18a. Which ages carry the pooled gap ===
  count-weighted average of the age-specific gaps: -0.1638, against the pooled estimate -0.1639
  ages 21-29   38.6% of filings   mean gap -0.0732    17.3% of the pooled gap
  ages 30-34   32.4% of filings   mean gap -0.1492    29.5% of the pooled gap
  ages 35-39   17.3% of filings   mean gap -0.2763    29.1% of the pooled gap
  ages 40-50   11.7% of filings   mean gap -0.3367    24.1% of the pooled gap
  Borjas's own Table 5 column 3 reports that the native seniority premium is small for the first ten years of job tenure and jumps after that. The omitted-tenure bias therefore grows with age, which is exactly the shape of this profile -- and the 3.6-point correction he applies is a single constant.

